## 📜 Multi-Tier Licensing & Intellectual Property Addendum

This repository operates under a unified, multi-tiered licensing framework to keep source code open and accessible while safeguarding creative works, datasets, and author attribution:

### 1. Code Attribution & Anti-Plagiarism Terms
- **Attribution Requirement:** Any distribution, fork, or public deployment of this Software must preserve all original copyright notices and explicitly credit **Mrityunjai** ([@Mrityunjai-hue](https://github.com/Mrityunjai-hue)) as the original creator.
- **Prohibition of Deceptive Re-Branding:** Users and distributors may not strip author credits, replace project logos, or re-publish this work under false authorship intended to deceive users or obscure original provenance.
- For complete legal definitions, refer to [COPYRIGHT_AND_INTELLECTUAL_PROPERTY.md](COPYRIGHT_AND_INTELLECTUAL_PROPERTY.md).

### 2. Creative Assets & Artwork (Creative Commons CC BY 4.0)
All visual UI themes, retro 8-bit icons, sound design audio effects (`playPaperclip()`, system chimes), forensic crime narratives, and documentation are licensed under the **Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0)**. You are free to share and adapt these materials with visible credit.

### 3. Schemas & Benchmark Question Sets (ODC-By v1.0)
All 130 LeetCode & HackerRank challenge question definitions, reference solutions, and simulated omni-domain relational schemas are licensed under the **Open Data Commons Attribution License (ODC-By v1.0)**.

### 4. Patent Grant Clause (Apache 2.0 Patent Terms)
Contributors and distributors grant users an express, perpetual, irrevocable patent license covering all self-made relational synthesis, AST schema inference, and multi-dialect transpilation algorithms embodied in the software.
